message: "If you use this book, please cite it as below."
title: "Bayesian Clinical Reasoning: Statistics, Decision Analysis, and Evidence for Neurologists and Clinician-Scientists"
abstract: >-
  A book on Bayesian clinical reasoning for neurology and related specialties.
  Twenty chapters move from probability language and Bayes' theorem through
  hierarchical models in R (brms) to decision analysis, net benefit, and
  shared decision-making.
type: software
authors:
  - name: Bayesian Clinical Reasoning contributors
url: "https://rkalani1.github.io/Bayesian-Reasoning/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/rkalani1/Bayesian-Reasoning"
keywords:
  - Bayesian statistics
  - clinical reasoning
  - decision analysis
  - neurology
  - stroke
  - medical education
  - brms
  - evidence-based medicine
